menu "NeuroEdge"

    config NEUROEDGE_SKIP_NETWORK
        bool "Do not bring up the Wi-Fi / TCP-IP stack"
        default n
        help
            For Espressif QEMU (sdkconfig.qemu, TSK-S4-08), which does not
            emulate Wi-Fi. The boot gate self-test still runs; the
            network_ready memory checkpoint is not taken. Leave this off on
            the board: the Q-3 measurement needs the network stack's cost.

    config NEUROEDGE_QEMU
        bool "This image runs on Espressif QEMU"
        default n
        help
            Set by sdkconfig.qemu (TSK-S4-09). Trace sessions then carry
            device_id "qemu", so evidence from the emulator never reads as
            evidence from the board; on the board device_id is the chip's MAC.

endmenu
